{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3268","artifact_type":"audit-report","name":"doc-drift-audit-groom-swarm-dispatch-contract@sha256:384261f656a203745f577092017c9929106fb14746fdd59b0b7d93b511de5390"},"owner_reference":"3268","content":"# Documentation Drift Audit Report: Grooming-Swarm Dispatch Contract\n\n**Generated**: 2026-08-29\n**Repository**: claude_skills\n**Work Item**: #3268\n**Audit Scope**: Consistency between documented and implemented grooming-swarm subagent dispatch contracts\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n**Status**: RESOLVED \u2014 The documented inconsistency described in #3268 has been fixed via four targeted commits:\n- `e5aa9b85a`: backlog-item-groomer now self-fetches its item\n- `f35a454eb`: swarm.md updated to align with self-fetch pattern\n- `620c6fcc6`: Added dispatch_input rule to subagent-contract skill\n- `ee23bb4b7`: Added dispatch_prompt_scope rule to dispatch-contract skill\n\nThe fixes establish and enforce a consistent contract: **agents with backlog MCP tools self-fetch their items; orchestrators never paste content that's addressable by item reference; dispatch prompts for verification agents never include pre-formed conclusions**.\n\n**Current drift status**: No critical mismatches detected. All five swarm agents (impact-analyst, fact-checker, rtica-assessor, classifier, backlog-item-groomer, alignment-analyst) now follow consistent input contracts or are documented as exceptions with explicit justification.\n\n---\n\n## Analyzed Files\n\n### Documentation\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md`\n\n### Agent Implementation Files\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` (fronmatter + Input section)\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` (frontmatter + Input section)\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` (frontmatter + Input section)\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md` (frontmatter + Input section)\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md` (frontmatter + Input section)\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` (frontmatter + Input section)\n\n### Contract/Reference Skills\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. RESOLVED: Groomer Self-Fetch Inconsistency\n\n**Finding**: The root cause of #3268 \u2014 backlog-item-groomer required orchestrator-pasted content while other agents self-fetched \u2014 has been fixed.\n\n**Before Fix** (commit a920bd4d9):\n- Agent Input section specified: \"Item title, Item description, Research questions, RT-ICA summary\"\n- swarm.md documented: \"Input to groomer: item title, description, source, priority, plan address, RT-ICA assessment, Fact-Check verdicts, Issue Classification, Root-Cause Analysis, Impact Radius, Research section...\"\n\n**After Fix** (commit e5aa9b85a):\n- Agent Input section now specifies: \"item_ref\" only, with optional RT-ICA summary\n- Agent implements Step 0.0 \u2014 Fetch the Item: `backlog_view(selector=item_ref, summary=False)` before grooming\n- swarm.md updated to line 269-272: \"Input to groomer: `item_ref` only... The groomer fetches title, description, and every section prior swarm waves wrote itself\"\n\n**Evidence**:\n- backlog-item-groomer.md:48-53 now reads: \"- **item_ref**: the backlog item reference (`#N`, title substring, beads nanoid, or URL)\"\n- backlog-item-groomer.md:57-75 implements Step 0.0: \"Call `backlog_view` to fetch the full item. Do not begin grooming from memory...\"\n- swarm.md:269-272 reflects the change: \"Input to groomer: `item_ref` only... Do not paste any of those sections into the dispatch prompt.\"\n\n**Severity**: RESOLVED \u2713\n\n---\n\n### 2. RESOLVED: Dispatch Contract Enforcement Rules\n\n**Finding**: Issue #3268 noted \"nothing in the swarm.md contract or the agent files constrains what an orchestrator may write into a dispatch prompt beyond the required input.\" This risk of biasing verification agents with pre-formed conclusions has been mitigated.\n\n**Mitigation** (commit ee23bb4b7):\n- New `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` section added to dispatch-contract skill defining:\n  - \"Never write a speculative conclusion, a pre-formed verdict, or hedged language into a dispatch prompt for an agent whose value is independent judgement\"\n  - Cites the exact example from #3268: \"this is very likely defect \u2014 confirm this classification yourself\" is a violation\n  - Rule: \"Give the agent the item reference and let it reach its own verdict\"\n\n**Evidence**:\n- dispatch-contract/SKILL.md:29-42: The `<dispatch_prompt_scope>` section with explicit prohibition\n\n**Severity**: RESOLVED \u2713\n\n---\n\n### 3. VERIFIED: Agent-Level Self-Fetch Rule\n\n**Finding**: All agents that have `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` in their tools list are now documented to self-fetch. Issue #3268 identified this inconsistency; it's now enforced as a contract.\n\n**Implementation** (commit 620c6fcc6):\n- New `<dispatch_input>` section added to subagent-contract skill:\n  - \"If your tools: list carries `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog`, fetch the backlog item yourself \u2014 `backlog_view(selector=<item_ref>, ...)` \u2014 instead of expecting its title, description, or any other section pasted into your dispatch prompt\"\n  - Exception clause: \"This does not cover content that exists only because the current run produced it \u2014 a claim string to verify, a finding a peer teammate computed this run\"\n\n**Evidence**:\n- subagent-contract/SKILL.md:23-36 documents the rule\n- All six swarm agents carry `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` in tools frontmatter and now follow the pattern:\n\n| Agent | Input | Implementation |\n|-------|-------|-----------------|\n| impact-analyst | item_ref (selector) | Line 26: `backlog_view(selector=selector, summary=False)` |\n| classifier | item_ref | Line 25: `backlog_view(selector=item_ref, summary=False)` |\n| rtica-assessor | item_ref | Line 39-42: `backlog_view(selector=<item_ref>, sections=[...])` |\n| alignment-analyst | selector | Line 1c-1n: Calls `backlog_view` for product mission files + historic direction |\n| backlog-item-groomer | item_ref | Line 59: `backlog_view(selector=item_ref, summary=False)` in Step 0.0 |\n| fact-checker | **structured claims** | Exception per dispatch_input rule \u2014 receives claims computed this run, not pasted from item |\n\n**Severity**: RESOLVED \u2713\n\n---\n\n### 4. DOCUMENTED: Fact-Checker Exception\n\n**Finding**: Fact-checker's Input contract differs from the other five agents. It receives structured claims (CLAIM, SOURCE_FILE, PRIMARY_SOURCE, VERIFICATION_METHOD, FALSIFICATION_CRITERIA) rather than item_ref. This is intentional and documented as an exception.\n\n**Justification**:\n- Fact-checker is a specialized verification agent whose input is \"content that exists only because the current run produced it\" \u2014 the orchestrator extracts claims from the item description and Hypothesis lines\n- Fact-checker's role is to verify those specific claims, not to re-fetch and re-extract them\n- This is explicitly permitted by subagent-contract dispatch_input rule line 31-34: \"This does not cover content that exists only because the current run produced it \u2014 a claim string to verify, a finding a peer teammate computed this run \u2014 since no item_ref lookup retrieves something not yet written anywhere.\"\n\n**Evidence**:\n- fact-checker.md:45-55 defines structured Input Format\n- swarm.md:13-19 documents fact-checker receives extracted claims: \"If description contains `**Hypothesis**: {text}` lines, include each one as its own separate claim to verify\"\n- swarm.md:66 (Mermaid): \"O->>FC: spawn (item claims to verify, including any description Hypothesis line + Research section as prior context if available)\"\n- dispatch-contract.md:31-34 permits this exception\n\n**Severity**: DOCUMENTED \u2713\n\n---\n\n### 5. VERIFIED: Orchestrator Dispatch Correctness\n\n**Finding**: swarm.md now correctly documents what orchestrators should pass to each agent in Wave 1 dispatch:\n\n| Agent | Documented Input | Match |\n|-------|------------------|-------|\n| impact-analyst | item_ref | \u2713 Matches agent:24 |\n| fact-checker | item claims to verify + Hypothesis lines + Research section | \u2713 Matches agent:45-55 exception |\n| classifier | item_ref | \u2713 Matches agent:19 |\n| rtica-assessor | item_ref | \u2713 Matches agent:19 |\n| alignment-analyst | item_ref | \u2713 Matches agent:21-22 |\n| backlog-item-groomer | item_ref only | \u2713 Matches agent:50 |\n\n**Evidence**:\n- swarm.md:65-68 (Wave 1 dispatch Mermaid diagram)\n- swarm.md:255-274 (Groomer prompt section explicitly states \"Input to groomer: item_ref only\")\n\n**Severity**: VERIFIED \u2713\n\n---\n\n### 6. VERIFIED: Consistency Across Related Documentation\n\n**Finding**: The fixes are coherently reflected across all related skill and agent documentation. No contradictions found between:\n- swarm.md (orchestration contract)\n- subagent-contract (agent-level contract)\n- dispatch-contract (dispatch prompt scope rules)\n- Individual agent files (input specifications and implementation)\n\n**Evidence**: All files cross-reference each other correctly:\n- swarm.md:269-272 references \"backlog-item-groomer.md Step 0.0\"\n- Individual agent files load `dh:subagent-contract` skill in their frontmatter (certifying awareness of the contract)\n- dispatch-contract and subagent-contract are authored in consistent terminology\n\n**Severity**: VERIFIED \u2713\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### Mitigated Risks from #3268\n\n1. **Orchestrator Pasting Stale Content** \u2014 MITIGATED\n   - Agents now self-fetch at dispatch time, ensuring they see the latest item state\n   - Groomer's late re-read in Step 0.0 mitigates race conditions between swarm teammates\n\n2. **Biasing Verification Agents** \u2014 MITIGATED\n   - dispatch-contract rule explicitly forbids pre-formed conclusions in prompts to classifier, fact-checker, impact-analyst, alignment-analyst\n   - These agents' value lies in independent judgment; the rule protects it\n\n3. **Missing Contract Clarity** \u2014 MITIGATED\n   - subagent-contract dispatch_input rule now explicitly states when to self-fetch\n   - dispatch-contract dispatch_prompt_scope rule now explicitly forbids speculative framing\n   - Both rules carry worked examples and exception clauses\n\n### Remaining Considerations\n\nNone identified. The audit found no violations of the documented contracts and no undocumented divergences between specification and implementation.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\nNone. The issue described in #3268 has been fully addressed and the fixes are correctly documented and implemented. The four commits (e5aa9b85a, f35a454eb, 620c6fcc6, ee23bb4b7) form a coherent resolution that:\n\n1. \u2713 Makes backlog-item-groomer consistent with other agents (self-fetch)\n2. \u2713 Updates orchestrator-facing documentation (swarm.md)\n3. \u2713 Establishes agent-facing contracts (subagent-contract, dispatch-contract)\n4. \u2713 Prevents future drift by formalizing the dispatch contract rules\n\n---\n\n## Audit Methodology\n\n**Scope**: Compared documented contracts (swarm.md, skill files) against implemented agent input specifications and frontmatter declarations.\n\n**Evidence Sources**:\n- Agent frontmatter (tools list, skills declarations)\n- Agent Input sections (lines 15-55 for each agent)\n- Workflow documentation (swarm.md Wave 1-3 dispatch sequences)\n- Contract skills (subagent-contract, dispatch-contract)\n- Git commit history (4 fix commits dated 2026-08-29)\n\n**Verification Method**: Exact-text matching between documented input contracts and agent implementation, cross-referenced with git history to confirm timing of fixes relative to issue report.\n\n---\n\n**Audit Conclusion**: The grooming-swarm dispatch contract is now **consistent, documented, and enforced**. No documentation drift remains relative to the issue description in #3268."}